[2026-08-03 15:45 AUSEST] rf2-digtt is now RULED (delegated dossier-review ruling, Mike's 2026-08-03 directive; operator-overturnable): carve-out IN — convergence suppressed during a live composition, one converge at compositionend, implemented as a composition shadow that also neutralises React's own restore (a bare isComposing skip is insufficient; see the ruling on rf2-digtt).

R-A2's IME clause should therefore claim, instead of the current false universal:
(1) the composing-commit fence — a composing Enter commits nothing — proven on all three implementations;
(2) for Hicasso's converge ONLY: composition survives value reassertion — a refused/normalised value is applied once, at compositionend (the rf2-digtt carve-out) — stated as deliberate divergence from the plain-React and UIx baselines, which abort the exchange mid-composition and must NOT have the property claimed for them;
(3) witness scope stated honestly: Chromium CDP; WebKit unwitnessed (composition driving is CDP-only).

Mind the tense: if this doc PR lands before the carve-out code does, word the Hicasso half as ruled-and-landing (tripwire: ime_run.cjs s5 rows), not as already-measured.
